# Empty guides: guide_none

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:giggly, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"}
  ])
```

## About this notebook

ggplot2's reference page for
[`guide_none()`](https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/guide_none.html) has no examples, so this
notebook says only what the page describes and where Giggly stands.

`guide_none()` is a guide that draws nothing. Given to a scale's `guide` argument or to `guides()`,
it leaves that scale without an axis or legend. Giggly writes it `:none`, in a scale's `guide:` or
in `Giggly.Plot.guides/2`, which leaves out a legend or colour bar, but has no `guide_none()` and no
way to leave out an axis.